invariant: INV-25
file: srv_parser_ext.c
catches: srv_test
reason: read_key_share stops requiring the entries to fill client_shares, so
  a list length that names fewer bytes than its one entry spans still yields
  that entry's share, and two encodings name one key_share. RFC 9846 §4.2.8
  frames the entries with that length.
  test/srv_parser_tests.h sends a 36-byte entry under a list length of 4,
  which fills the extension body exactly, so the exact-fill check after the
  reader cannot refuse it first.

--- old
        used += 4 + share_len;
    }
    if (used != list_len) {
        return srv_refuse(p->alert, ALERT_DECODE_ERROR);
    }
    return CH_OK;
--- new
        used += 4 + share_len;
    }
    return CH_OK;
